# Build outputs and run scratch are regenerable; findings and the committed
# seed set are the deliverable and are NOT ignored.
build/
runs/
third_party/
corpus/external/
# The per-target grown/ratcheted corpus is regenerable from a campaign + ratchet.
corpus/*/evolved/
# The curated seed set ships as ONE archive (corpus/seeds.tar.gz), unpacked by
# `make corpus`. The extracted per-target dirs are NOT committed (thousands of
# small files); only the archive + MANIFEST.toml + sources.toml are tracked.
corpus/decode/
corpus/encode/
corpus/md5/
# Per-target libFuzzer working corpora (corpus/fz_*/): the fleet seeds each from the
# decode/encode/md5 sets above (config.py corpus=...) and grows them in place; the
# distilled result is carried forward under corpus/fz_*/evolved/ (already ignored).
# Neither the working files nor their evolved distillate are committed -- regenerable
# from `make corpus` + a campaign + `scripts/ratchet.sh`.
corpus/fz_*/
# Raw per-run divergence dumps (witness-config buckets); curated reproducers live
# in findings/. Regenerable by re-running a campaign.
divergences/
# Generated llvm-cov reports (profdata / native.txt / HTML); regenerated by
# `make coverage` / cov/per_target.py.
cov/report/
*.mapsize
__pycache__/
.tmp/
# libFuzzer/AFL artifact files can be dropped in the tree by an ad-hoc run; never
# commit them (curated reproducers live in findings/).
crash-*
leak-*
oom-*
timeout-*
slow-unit-*
